=== epam Output (attempt 1) ===
The test failure indicates that the truncate function isn't properly handling the custom suffix case when the text length exactly matches maxLength. Let's fix this by modifying the truncate function to handle this edge case correctly.

Here's the corrected implementation:

```typescript
export function truncate(text: string, maxLength: number, suffix: string = '...'): string {
  if (text.length <= maxLength) return text;
  if (maxLength <= 0) return suffix;
  
  const truncLength = Math.max(0, maxLength - suffix.length);
  if (truncLength === 0) return suffix;
  
  return text.slice(0, truncLength) + suffix;
}
```

The key changes are:
1. Added explicit handling for the case where truncLength becomes 0 after subtracting suffix length
2. Simplified the logic to ensure proper truncation with custom suffixes

